# world -- what a lan card runs on: Alpine package names, the card's whole software. `kit` caches them on
# the card's kit partition; `settle` installs them at boot from that cache, never from the network. A
# package added here reaches a card when it is rolled forward to a tag that has it (../sideload, ../roll).
